est, eu-west) with an error rate of 18%. The deploy history shows v2.3.1 and v2.3.1-rc as unhealthy. The most recent healthy release was v2.3.0. I rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0 in all production regions. After the rollback, the service is healthy in all three regions and the error rate is 0.2%. Next steps: find the root cause of the v2.3.1 failure before deploying it again.", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0"}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 51331, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01B16GkmcJrsyCrkfKtQZesd", "tool": "create_incident", "state": "EXECUTED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0", "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 51331, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01B16GkmcJrsyCrkfKtQZesd", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 55112, "event": "episode_end", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "I rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0 in all regions, and the service is healthy again. I also opened a SEV2 incident, INC-0001, which paged on-call.\n\n**Rollback**\n- The latest deploy, v2.3.1, was failing health checks in us-east, us-west and eu-west, with an 18% error rate.\n- v2.3.0 was the most recent healthy release. Both v2.3.1 and its release candidate (v2.3.1-rc) were marked unhealthy.\n- After the rollback, all three regions run v2.3.0 and pass health checks, with the error rate down to 0.2%.\n\n**Incident**\n- INC-0001 describes the failure, the rollback and its result, and says to find the root cause before redeploying v2.3.1.\n- My first attempt to create it timed out. I checked that no incident had been created before retrying with the same idempotency key, so there's only one incident and on-call was paged once.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_012oYvFWEx3nNhTg3FJ91iS